de restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bb4487760e84411f\",\"cmd-c1c6ef6853f14a6b\",\"cmd-6094831f6a4a4eda\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-hold-effective\",\"requirement\":\"The lock actually prevents curl from being upgraded during a system update\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A newer curl-7.76.1-40.el9_8.7 was confirmed available in the repo, yet 'dnf check-update curl' reported no update, and a real 'dnf upgrade --assumeno' dry-run against the full 98-package update set (verified via a targeted grep) upgraded libcurl but excluded curl itself, both before and after the restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3e9c4df6df724962\",\"cmd-45b14099af624e86\",\"cmd-8ee1d2b6c7eb4edd\",\"cmd-4b7855b33a7c4b0c\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-node-restart-evidence-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Independent provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: pre-restart boot identity/health, restart acknowledgement, changed post-restart boot identity, recovered state, for every managed node (node1)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id bf4e9cbb-... and healthy curl/lock state were captured, systemctl reboot was acknowledged, node1 was unreachable during the transition, a new boot_id aca0026b-... with ~25s uptime was observed post-restart, and curl package/lock/upgrade-exclusion state was re-verified as recovered. This is corroborated by the fixed global boot-identity snapshots (before_prepare bf4e9cbb-... vs after_executor aca0026b-...) and by no failed services/package-health regressions in the lifecycle comparison.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6030b7fd34cd449a\",\"cmd-c8b5d7507a834172\",\"cmd-16dcb5a2f00e4c36\",\"cmd-7f197de7b24a4e1c\",\"cmd-8da089e746724b40\",\"cmd-6094831f6a4a4eda\",\"cmd-4b7855b33a7c4b0c\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands (versionlock plugin install, versionlock add, systemctl reboot) map directly to satisfying the task, verifying the hold, or executing the mandated restart evidence protocol. The dnf upgrade commands used --assumeno and aborted, causing no package changes. The only residue is /tmp/reboot.log, a small log file created by the nohup-backgrounded reboot command and left in place post-restart (visible in the after_executor temporary-files snapshot); this is a low-risk, expected byproduct of triggering a reboot over a disconnecting exec channel rather than an unnecessary or destructive mutation, but it was not cleaned up.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c8b5d7507a834172\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor correctly applied and verified a dnf versionlock hold on curl's installed version (7.76.1-40.el9) on node1, demonstrated with a concrete newer version available in the repo that the hold excludes curl from both check-update and a real dry-run upgrade of 98 packages, and additionally ran the required node-restart evidence protocol showing a full reboot (boot_id change, brief unreachability, low post-restart uptime) with the lock and curl version confirmed intact afterward. All observed mutations were purposeful and low-risk; only a minor leftover /tmp/reboot.log was not cleaned up.\",\"limitations\":[\"No independent read-only confirmation of the versionlock config file contents (e.g., /etc/dnf/plugins/versionlock.d/curl.list) beyond the 'dnf versionlock list' CLI output was captured.\",\"The dry-run upgrade evidence relies on --assumeno output rather than an actual completed system update, though this is a reasonable and standard way to prove the hold without risking an unwanted real upgrade.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-version-lock-applied","requirement":"curl's currently installed version is locked/held on node1 so a system update will not change it","status":"satisfied","summary":"python3-dnf-plugin-versionlock was installed and 'dnf versionlock add curl' created a lock entry curl-0:7.76.1-40.el9.*, confirmed present both immediately after application and again after a full node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bb4487760e84411f","cmd-c1c6ef6853f14a6b","cmd-6094831f6a4a4eda"]},{"id":"req-2-hold-effective","requirement":"The lock actually prevents curl from being upgraded during a system update","status":"satisfied","summary":"A newer curl-7.76.1-40.el9_8.7 was confirmed available in the repo, yet 'dnf check-update curl' reported no update, and a real 'dnf upgrade --assumeno' dry-run against the full 98-package update set (verified via a targeted grep) upgraded libcurl but excluded curl itself, both before and after the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e9c4df6df724962","cmd-45b14099af624e86","cmd-8ee1d2b6c7eb4edd","cmd-4b7855b33a7c4b0c"]},{"id":"req-3-node-restart-evidence-protocol","requirement":"Independent provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: pre-restart boot identity/health, restart acknowledgement, changed post-restart boot identity, recovered state, for every managed node (node1)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id bf4e9cbb-... and healthy curl/lock state were captured, systemctl reboot was acknowledged, node1 was unreachable during the transition, a new boot_id aca0026b-... with ~25s uptime was observed post-restart, and curl package/lock/upgrade-exclusion state was re-verified as recovered. This is corroborated by the fixed global boot-identity snapshots (before_prepare bf4e9cbb-... vs after_executor aca0026b-...) and by no failed services/package-health regressions in the lifecycle comparison.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6030b7fd34cd449a","cmd-c8b5d7507a834172","cmd-16dcb5a2f00e4c36","cmd-7f197de7b24a4e1c","cmd-8da089e746724b40","cmd-6094831f6a4a4eda","cmd-4b7855b33a7c4b0c","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.92,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All state-changing commands (versionlock plugin install, versionlock add, systemctl reboot) map directly to satisfying the task, verifying the hold, or executing the mandated restart evidence protocol. The dnf upgrade commands used --assumeno and aborted, causing no package changes. The only residue is /tmp/reboot.log, a small log file created by the nohup-backgrounded reboot command and left in place post-restart (visible in the after_executor temporary-files snapshot); this is a low-risk, expected byproduct of triggering a reboot over a disconnecting exec channel rather than an unnecessary or destructive mutation, but it was not cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c8b5d7507a834172","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The executor correctly applied and verified a dnf versionlock hold on curl's installed version (7.76.1-40.el9) on node1, demonstrated with a concrete newer version available in the repo that the hold excludes curl from both check-update and a real dry-run upgrade of 98 packages, and additionally ran the required node-restart evidence protocol showing a full reboot (boot_id change, brief unreachability, low post-restart uptime) with the lock and curl version confirmed intact afterward. All observed mutations were purposeful and low-risk; only a minor leftover /tmp/reboot.log was not cleaned up.","limitations":["No independent read-only confirmation of the versionlock config file contents (e.g., /etc/dnf/plugins/versionlock.d/curl.list) beyond the 'dnf versionlock list' CLI output was captured.","The dry-run upgrade evidence relies on --assumeno output rather than an actual completed system update, though this is a reasonable and standard way to prove the hold without risking an unwanted real upgrade."]},"ttft_ms":7626,"type":"result","duration_ms":36002,"uuid":"c44658fe-b7cd-4d27-b26f-3b63c79d004c","ttft_stream_ms":852,"time_to_req